invariant: INV-45
file: src/sha3_inverted_lanes.h
catches: sha3_equiv_test
reason: the second round of each two writes the state it reads, where it
  reads the scratch state and writes the caller's. A row's five stores
  then change lanes that a later row reads, so the round is no longer
  the standard's. The equivalence test runs the inverted lanes form on
  every machine and requires the reference's state.

--- old
        keccak_round_inverted(a, scratch, rc[1]);
--- new
        keccak_round_inverted(a, a, rc[1]);
